ne directly.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_006"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "name": "Serine thermolysis route", "description": "Hydrothermal retro-aldol decomposition of serine yields glycine and formaldehyde.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_007"], "key_intermediates": []}, {"pathway_id": "P8", "name": "Serine-to-aminonitrile relay", "description": "Serine thermolysis liberates formaldehyde; after transport into a cyanosulfidic surface pool it can be trapped as aminoacetonitrile and hydrolyzed to an additional glycine equivalent.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_007", "rxn_001", "rxn_002"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_003", "mol_006"]}, {"pathway_id": "P9", "name": "Strecker-peracid tandem route", "description": "Surface Strecker chemistry yields aminoacetonitrile and then glycine; the ammonia released on hydrolysis can be recaptured by hydrothermal peracetic acid to generate a second glycine equivalent.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_006"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_006", "mol_005"]}, {"pathway_id": "P10", "name": "Serine-driven multi-module glycine amplification", "description": "A hydrothermal-surface-hydrothermal relay: serine decomposition supplies formaldehyde for Strecker aminonitrile formation, and the hydrolysis-released ammonia is then reused in peracetic acid amination, giving three glycine equivalents overall.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_007", "rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_006"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_003", "mol_006", "mol_005"]}], "hub_molecules": ["mol_001", "mol_002", "mol_003", "mol_005", "mol_006", "mol_007"], "convergence_points": [{"molecule_id": "mol_003", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_007"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_001"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_005", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_002"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_001", "rxn_006"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_006", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_001"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_002"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_007", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_003", "rxn_005"], "outgoing_